<title>CANADA: Canada Flax Council forecasts 1996/97 world output.</title>
<headline>Canada Flax Council forecasts 1996/97 world output.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>World flaxseed output was forecast to decline 12.3 percent in crop year 1996/97 (Aug/July) with the drop in production coming mainly from Canada and Argentina, the Flax Council of Canada said at its annual meeting here on Tuesday.</p>
<p>		 WORLD FLAXSEED PRODUCTION (million tonnes)</p>
<p>Country  1996/97 F 1995/96  1994/95  1990/94 Avg</p>
<p>Canada     0.86	 1.11    0.96    0.69</p>
<p>China	0.40	 0.40    0.42    0.44</p>
<p>India	0.34	 0.34    0.33    0.31</p>
<p>EU-15	0.21	 0.19    0.16    0.22</p>
<p>FSU	  0.11	 0.12    0.11    0.14</p>
<p>Argentina  0.09	 0.15    0.15    0.25</p>
<p>U.S.A.     0.05	 0.06    0.07    0.10</p>
<p>East Europe0.05	 0.05    0.05    0.05</p>
<p>Other	0.18	 0.19    0.19    0.18</p>
<p>Total:     2.29	 2.61    2.44    2.38</p>
<p>Source -- Oil World and Agriculture Canada</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
</text>
